REPLACE_ME_WITH_YOUR_APPLE_PAY_DOMAIN_ASSOCIATION_TOKEN

This file is a PLACEHOLDER. Apple Pay will not work until it is replaced.

What it is
  Apple's domain-verification token. Apple fetches
  https://<your-domain>/.well-known/apple-developer-merchantid-domain-association
  and compares the body byte-for-byte with the token it issued.

How to replace it
  1. Register this exact domain with your Apple Pay merchant identifier
     (via Solidgate's dashboard, or directly in the Apple Developer portal).
  2. Download the association file it gives you.
  3. Overwrite this file with its contents. No trailing edits, no reformatting —
     the body is compared exactly.
  4. Re-issue it per merchant AND per domain. A token minted for the staging
     domain will not verify production.

Do not move or rename this path
  next.config.ts pins a `Content-Type: text/plain` header on it (the file is
  extensionless, so Next would otherwise serve application/octet-stream and
  verification fails), and src/proxy.ts excludes /.well-known/ from the auth
  gate because Apple and Solidgate fetch it unauthenticated.
